427
00:26:38,084 --> 00:26:41,269
The ones who, make Jihad(جهاد) in My cause

428
00:26:41,555 --> 00:26:43,737
We will surely guide them to Our paths.

429
00:26:44,119 --> 00:26:47,610
So this is not specifically talking about fighting it's talking in the general sense.

430
00:26:50,466 --> 00:26:53,140
and the Ayah(آية) in Surah Luqman(سورة لقمان)

431
00:26:53,170 --> 00:26:57,072
وَإِن جَاهَدَاكَ عَلَىٰ أَن تُشْرِكَ بِي مَا لَيْسَ لَكَ بِهِ عِلْمٌ فَلَا تُطِعْهُمَا ۖ

432
00:26:57,341 --> 00:27:00,435
It's the same as Ayah(آية) before a referring to the parents.

433
00:27:01,150 --> 00:27:02,173
So these Ayaat(آيات) are clear.!

434
00:27:03,547 --> 00:27:06,168
Tayeb(طيِّب) in Madina Jihad(جهاد) is mentioned 26 times

435
00:27:06,709 --> 00:27:11,161
and invariably they are referring to fighting in the sake of Allah,

436
00:27:13,264 --> 00:27:16,368
And this is final meaning of Jihad(جهاد).

437
00:27:17,424 --> 00:27:24,208
I'm saying this because nowadays it is very common

438
00:27:25,248 --> 00:27:28,478
to find among Muslims, the understanding

439
00:27:29,351 --> 00:27:33,758
that Jihad(جهاد) is primarily Jihad An-Nafs(جهاد النفس)

440
00:27:34,957 --> 00:27:40,528
and the secondary meaning is the fighting with Kuffar(كفار).

441
00:27:40,644 --> 00:27:45,663
And the Hadith(حديث) is always quoted in this context:

442
00:27:46,361 --> 00:27:51,496
We came back from the minor Jihad(جهاد) to Major Jihad(جهاد),

443
00:27:51,996 --> 00:27:52,996
Jihad-Un-Nafs(جهاد النفس).

444
00:27:53,996 --> 00:27:57,993
Now, first of all this Hadith(حديث) as Ibn Taymiyah(اِبْنِ تَيْمِيَّه) says, is fabricated.

445
00:28:01,845 --> 00:28:08,131
Nevertheless, you will still find that this is quite a common belief.

446
00:28:12,357 --> 00:28:13,809
But if we look at the Ayaat(آيات),

447
00:28:14,523 --> 00:28:17,428
we'd find that the Ayah(آية) would only make sense

448
00:28:19,867 --> 00:28:21,711
if Jihad(جهاد) is interpreted as fighting.

449
00:28:23,201 --> 00:28:24,201
For example

450
00:28:25,153 --> 00:28:27,692
the Ayah(آية) in Surah At-Tauba(سورة التوبة) Verse 41.

451
00:28:29,470 --> 00:28:31,470
ٱنفِرُواْ خِفَافًا وَثِقَالًا

452
00:28:32,065 --> 00:28:35,199
وَجَٰهِدُواْ بِأَمْوَٰلِكُمْ وَأَنفُسِكُمْ فِى سَبِيلِ ٱللَّهِ ۚ

453
00:28:35,835 --> 00:28:39,652
March forth, whether you are light or heavy

454
00:28:40,454 --> 00:28:44,574
and strive hard with your wealth and your lives, in the cause of Allah.

455
00:28:45,169 --> 00:28:47,994
How come this Ayah(آية) will only make sense if it's refer to fighting.

456
00:28:50,003 --> 00:28:51,312
Again the Ayah(آية), March forth

457
00:28:51,845 --> 00:28:56,122
whether you are light or heavy and strive hard with your wealth and your lives in the cause of Allah.

458
00:28:57,182 --> 00:28:59,825
How come it only make sense if it's refer to fighting?

459
00:29:01,531 --> 00:29:04,236
Infiroo(اِنْفِرُو), the Ayah(آية) is saying March forth.

460
00:29:04,737 --> 00:29:07,736
Jihad Un-Nafs(جهاد النفس) doesn't need marching forth,

461
00:29:08,261 --> 00:29:10,819
the Jihad(جهاد) of Shaytan(شَيْطَانْ) doesn't need marching forth.

462
00:29:12,647 --> 00:29:15,933
The Jihad(جهاد) of the Munafiqeen(مُنافقين) within the ranks doesn't need marching forth.

463
00:29:16,640 --> 00:29:19,004
You fight them right then in neighborhood, you doesn't have to go out.

464
00:29:19,925 --> 00:29:22,095
So The Ayah(آية) would only make sense

465
00:29:22,120 --> 00:29:24,215
- if it is talking about the Jihad bil Kufar(جهاد بالکفار),

466
00:29:26,931 --> 00:29:27,951
The next Ayah(آية)

467
00:29:28,616 --> 00:29:31,822
فَرِحَ ٱلْمُخَلَّفُونَ بِمَقْعَدِهِمْ خِلَٰفَ رَسُولِ ٱللَّهِ

468
00:29:32,172 --> 00:29:37,025
وَكَرِهُواْ أَن يُجَٰهِدُواْ بِأَمْوَٰلِهِمْ وَأَنفُسِهِمْ فِى سَبِيلِ ٱللَّهِ وَقَالُواْ لَا تَنفِرُواْ فِى ٱلْحَرِّ ۗ

469
00:29:37,367 --> 00:29:40,999
قُلْ نَارُ جَهَنَّمَ أَشَدُّ حَرًّا ۚ لَّوْ كَانُواْ يَفْقَهُونَ۝

470
00:29:41,338 --> 00:29:45,082
Those who stayed away, rejoice and they're staying behind the Messenger of Allah.

471
00:29:45,594 --> 00:29:50,043
They hated to strive with their properties and their lives in the cause of Allah. And they said:

472
00:29:50,475 --> 00:29:52,512
March, not forth in the heat,

473
00:29:53,045 --> 00:29:55,028
say, the fire of hell is more intense in heat.

474
00:29:55,505 --> 00:29:57,100
 If only they could understand.

475
00:29:59,211 --> 00:30:00,646
This was in the battle of Tabook(تبوك).

476
00:30:01,448 --> 00:30:02,827
It was summer

477
00:30:03,764 --> 00:30:12,169
It was right before the harvest, which means that thefood level at its slowest right before the harvest.

478
00:30:13,192 --> 00:30:17,481
And it's about to be at its highest, if they would stay behind for harvest.

479
00:30:18,743 --> 00:30:21,234
And this would be the longest journey ever

480
00:30:21,327 --> 00:30:24,688
because they are going from Madina all the way to the Roman empire, Tabook(تبوك).

481
00:30:26,156 --> 00:30:31,718
And its fighting with a Very formidable enemies, the Romans.

482
00:30:32,861 --> 00:30:34,844
So this was a serious challenge.

483
00:30:35,504 --> 00:30:40,858
This is really the test of the true Eeman(ايمان) and Nifaq(نِفاق)

484
00:30:40,940 --> 00:30:44,255
 that's when the Munafiqeen(مُنافقين) truly showed their color, it was in Ghazwa Tabuk(غزوة التبوك).

485
00:30:44,872 --> 00:30:47,856
Because all the elements were against the Munafiqeen(مُنافقين),

486
00:30:48,650 --> 00:30:50,094
the challenge was too big for them.

487
00:30:51,356 --> 00:30:54,269
So they told Rasool Allah ﷺ,

488
00:30:54,372 --> 00:30:57,188
these are excuses we can't go, everyone came up with an excuse.

489
00:30:57,738 --> 00:30:59,580
So, when Rasool Allah ﷺ left - they were happy.

490
00:30:59,611 --> 00:31:00,435
فَرِحَ ٱلْمُخَلَّفُونَ

491
00:31:00,468 --> 00:31:02,821
They were happy that they stayed behind, they rejoiced.

492
00:31:03,672 --> 00:31:05,926
And they said: Don't go out, it's too hot.

493
00:31:06,402 --> 00:31:12,302
Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ is telling them that Jahannum(جَهَّنَّم) is hotter that the summer of Arabia.

494
00:31:14,116 --> 00:31:15,854
But this Ayah(آية) can only mean,

495
00:31:15,887 --> 00:31:18,237
Jihad(جهاد) - in this Ayah(آية) can only mean - going out,

496
00:31:19,339 --> 00:31:21,745
and the other Ayah(آية) also in Surat Touba(سورةالتوبة) verse 86.

497
00:31:21,761 --> 00:31:25,451
وَإِذَا أُنزِلَتْ سُورَةٌ أَنْ ءَامِنُواْ بِٱللَّهِ وَجَٰهِدُواْ مَعَ رَسُولِهِ

498
00:31:25,483 --> 00:31:27,022
ٱسْتَـْٔذَنَكَ أُوْلُواْ ٱلطَّوْلِ مِنْهُمْ

499
00:31:27,190 --> 00:31:29,380
وَقَالُواْ ذَرْنَا نَكُن مَّعَ ٱلْقَٰعِدِينَ۝

500
00:31:30,205 --> 00:31:31,705
And when Surah(سورة) is revealed

501
00:31:31,920 --> 00:31:36,824
enjoining them to believe in Allah and to make Jihad(جهاد) with the Messenger of Allah.

502
00:31:37,106 --> 00:31:39,322
The wealthy among them ask you,

503
00:31:39,361 --> 00:31:43,288
leave to exempt them and they say, leave us behind,

504
00:31:43,590 --> 00:31:45,300
we would be with those who sit home.

505
00:31:46,421 --> 00:31:49,041
See the wealthy are always hesitant to go.

506
00:31:52,341 --> 00:31:54,167
What about the Hadith(حديث) of Rasool Allah ﷺ?

507
00:31:56,575 --> 00:31:56,933
Tayeb(طيِّب)

508
00:31:57,494 --> 00:32:01,701
Abu Hurairah(ابوهريره) says and this Hadith(حديث) is in Muslim(مسلم).

509
00:32:03,867 --> 00:32:05,470
Rasool Allah ﷺ was asked,

510
00:32:06,887 --> 00:32:09,236
Is there any deed equivalent to Jihad(جهاد)?

511
00:32:10,380 --> 00:32:11,800
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: Yes!

512
00:32:11,832 --> 00:32:13,400
But you won't be able to do it.

513
00:32:15,552 --> 00:32:16,805
So the man asked again,

514
00:32:17,322 --> 00:32:18,450
he asked the third time,

515
00:32:18,474 --> 00:32:20,466
Rasool Allah ﷺ told him third time.

516
00:32:20,823 --> 00:32:22,616
What is equivalent to the Mujahid(مُجَاهِد),

517
00:32:23,069 --> 00:32:26,398
is the one who is fasting and praying continuously.

518
00:32:26,636 --> 00:32:28,350
Until the Mujahid(مُجَاهِد) comes back.

519
00:32:29,494 --> 00:32:33,304
How come this Hadith(حديث) is only mean fighting.

520
00:32:35,829 --> 00:32:38,913
What is in this Hadith(حديث) that tells you straight away

521
00:32:39,317 --> 00:32:40,817
that this can only mean fighting.

522
00:32:42,719 --> 00:32:43,632
Comes back!

523
00:32:43,822 --> 00:32:44,544
Comes back!

524
00:32:44,680 --> 00:32:46,528
He came back, the Mujahid(مُجَاهِد) came back.

525
00:32:47,315 --> 00:32:50,907
So you're praying and fasting, until the Mujahid(مُجَاهِد) comes back.

526
00:32:52,392 --> 00:32:54,580
So the one who's staying behind is actually doing what??

527
00:32:55,463 --> 00:32:56,439
Jihad(جهاد) of What?

528
00:32:56,701 --> 00:32:57,439
Jihad An Nafs(جهاد بالنفس)!!!

529
00:32:58,693 --> 00:33:01,804
The one who's staying behind praying and fasting.

530
00:33:02,731 --> 00:33:03,911
He is doing Jihad An Nafs(جهاد بالنفس)..…

531
00:33:04,765 --> 00:33:06,639
So Rasool Allah ﷺ is saying that,

532
00:33:06,862 --> 00:33:11,106
this person who is doing Jihad An Nafs(جهاد بالنفس) even if he's praying all the night, fasting everyday

533
00:33:11,584 --> 00:33:15,160
 is not gonna get near, to the one who goes out for Jihad(جهاد) Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله).

534
00:33:17,554 --> 00:33:18,752
The next Hadith(حديث)

535
00:33:19,657 --> 00:33:21,117
Rasool Allah ﷺ was asked

536
00:33:21,554 --> 00:33:23,630
guide me to a deed equivalent to Jihad(جهاد)?

537
00:33:23,662 --> 00:33:25,455
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: I don’t find any,

538
00:33:25,599 --> 00:33:26,319
then he said:

539
00:33:26,813 --> 00:33:29,849
When the Mujahid(مُجَاهِد) goes on Jihad(جهاد), so now he's going,

540
00:33:30,339 --> 00:33:32,770
can you enter your Masjid(مسجد) and pray continuously

541
00:33:32,787 --> 00:33:34,671
and fast and never break your fast.

542
00:33:34,949 --> 00:33:37,139
The man said: And who could do that.

543
00:33:37,631 --> 00:33:39,052
 And this is in Bukhari(بخاريْ).

544
00:33:40,036 --> 00:33:41,373
Third Hadith(حديث),

545
00:33:42,802 --> 00:33:44,159
Rasool Allah ﷺ said,

546
00:33:45,548 --> 00:33:47,032
after he was asked:

547
00:33:47,064 --> 00:33:48,469
What is the best Jihad(جهاد)?

548
00:33:48,985 --> 00:33:52,302
So now the question is placed straightforward to Rasul Ullah:

549
00:33:52,429 --> 00:33:53,429
What's the best Jihad(جهاد).?

550
00:33:53,540 --> 00:33:54,595
What's the major Jihad(جهاد)?

551
00:33:54,881 --> 00:33:56,825
See sometime if you look at the Sahih Hadith(صحيح حديث)

552
00:33:56,859 --> 00:33:57,756
you would find the answer.

553
00:33:58,177 --> 00:33:59,184
So this Hadith(حديث),

554
00:33:59,820 --> 00:34:01,949
the man is asking Rasul Ullah, what is the best Jihad(جهاد)?

555
00:34:02,005 --> 00:34:03,605
Rasool Allah ﷺ said:

556
00:34:03,847 --> 00:34:07,500
من عقر جوادہ ، وأریق دمه

557
00:34:08,089 --> 00:34:11,001
The ones, whose horse is killed and his blood spilled.

558
00:34:11,653 --> 00:34:12,728
So that is the best Jihad(جهاد).

559
00:34:12,796 --> 00:34:16,218
The ones whose horse is killed and his blood is spilled.

560
00:34:16,812 --> 00:34:18,751
So this is in the context of fighting.

561
00:34:19,026 --> 00:34:21,699
And Rasool Allah ﷺ says that it is the best.

562
00:34:22,936 --> 00:34:25,298
Ibn Abbas(إبن عباس) narrates that the Messenger of Allah said:

563
00:34:27,448 --> 00:34:29,708
When your brothers were killed at Uhud(أحَد)

564
00:34:30,794 --> 00:34:33,927
Allah placed their souls in the insides of green birds.

565
00:34:35,150 --> 00:34:37,532
These birds drink from the rivers of Paradise,

566
00:34:38,225 --> 00:34:42,720
and eat from its fruits, and travel in paradise wherever they want.

567
00:34:43,644 --> 00:34:44,644
So they said:

568
00:34:44,842 --> 00:34:47,986
We wish our people knew what Allah has given us.

569
00:34:48,399 --> 00:34:51,120
- So they would desire Jihad(جهاد) and not neglect it.

570
00:34:52,305 --> 00:34:53,425
So over here,

571
00:34:53,829 --> 00:34:56,874
the Sahabah(صحابه) the Shuhadaa(شُهَدآء) of Uhud(أحَد) are saying in Jannah(جنة),

572
00:34:57,269 --> 00:35:03,435
we wish that the pleasure that we are in, is conveyed to our people.

573
00:35:03,928 --> 00:35:05,406
So they will not neglect Jihad(جهاد).

574
00:35:06,535 --> 00:35:09,622
Notice here that they just said Jihad(جهاد), they didn't add a clause to it.

575
00:35:10,075 --> 00:35:12,705
To define whether it is Jihad An Nafs(جهاد بالنفس) or Jihad(جهاد)…

576
00:35:13,415 --> 00:35:15,215
They just said: Jihad(جهاد)

577
00:35:17,034 --> 00:35:20,122
Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ said: I will convey that to your brothers.

578
00:35:20,416 --> 00:35:22,487
So they became very pleased. And that's when Allah

579
00:35:22,503 --> 00:35:24,352
revealed the Ayaat(آيات) of Surah Al-Imran(سورة ألعمران)

580
00:35:24,789 --> 00:35:27,512
from Ayah(آية) Verse 169 to 171.

581
00:35:27,781 --> 00:35:29,138
Talking about the Shuhadaa(شُهَدآء),

582
00:35:29,226 --> 00:35:31,867
and don't consider the ones who died in the sake of Allah

583
00:35:31,931 --> 00:35:33,621
as dead, but they're alive.

584
00:35:34,026 --> 00:35:41,051
وَلا تَحْسَبَنَّ الَّذِينَ قُتِلُوا فِي سَبِيلِ اللَّهِ أَمْواتًا

585
00:35:41,109 --> 00:35:45,806
بَلْ أَحْياءٌ عِنْدَ رَبِّهِمْ يُرْزَقُونَ ۞

586
00:35:46,406 --> 00:35:52,053
فَرِحِينَ بِمَا آتَاهُمُ اللَّهُ مِن فَضْلِهِ

587
00:35:52,421 --> 00:35:58,383
وَيَسْتَبْشِرُونَ بالَّذِينَ لَمْ يَلْحَقُوا بِهِم مِّنْ خَلْفِهِمْ

588
00:35:58,649 --> 00:36:03,473
أَلَّا خَوْفٌ عَلَيْهِمْ وَلَا هُمْ يَحْزَنُونَ ۞

589
00:36:03,904 --> 00:36:15,438
يَسْتَبْشِرُونَ بِنِعْمَةٍ مِّنَ اللَّهِ وَفَضْلٍ وَأَنَّ اللَّهَ لَا يُضِيعُ أَجْرَ الْمُؤْمِنِينَ ۞

590
00:36:20,805 --> 00:36:24,489
Abu Hurairah(ابوهريره) narrates that one of the companions passed by a fresh

591
00:36:25,376 --> 00:36:27,829
 by a spring of fresh water in the valley.

592
00:36:28,314 --> 00:36:30,876
He said: If I seclude myself from the people,

593
00:36:31,165 --> 00:36:33,183
and stay in this valley to worship Allah.

594
00:36:33,841 --> 00:36:35,864
So this man wanted to do Jihad An Nafs(جهاد بالنفس),

595
00:36:36,416 --> 00:36:38,838
stay next to this fountain of water,

596
00:36:39,370 --> 00:36:42,300
devoting himself to the Ibadah(عبادة) of Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ full time,

597
00:36:42,730 --> 00:36:43,870
 stay away from the sins,

598
00:36:44,171 --> 00:36:45,213
 stay away from people.

599
00:36:46,058 --> 00:36:48,571
But he wanted to seek permission from the Rasool Allah ﷺ first.

600
00:36:49,628 --> 00:36:51,462
So he went to Rasul Ullah and he asked him,

601
00:36:52,011 --> 00:36:54,218
Rasool Allah ﷺ told him: Don't do so.

602
00:36:56,714 --> 00:36:58,104
And then Rasool Allah ﷺ said:

603
00:36:58,542 --> 00:37:01,268
The posting of one of you in the path of Allah

604
00:37:01,960 --> 00:37:05,045
is better than his prayer in his house for 70 years.

605
00:37:05,890 --> 00:37:08,975
Don't you want Allah to forgive you and enter you into paradise.

606
00:37:09,749 --> 00:37:10,118
Fight!

607
00:37:10,181 --> 00:37:11,751
And Rasul Ullah use the word Ughoo(اُغْزوا)

608
00:37:12,040 --> 00:37:14,384
in the path of Allah, for whoever fights

609
00:37:14,592 --> 00:37:15,061
قاتَل

610
00:37:15,142 --> 00:37:16,266
in the path of Allah,

611
00:37:16,283 --> 00:37:18,689
a time equivalent to that of milking camel,

612
00:37:19,038 --> 00:37:20,730
paradise is guaranteed for him.

613
00:37:21,629 --> 00:37:22,941
This Hadith(حديث) is in At-Tirmidhi(ألتِّرمِذِيْ).

614
00:37:25,222 --> 00:37:27,203
Tayeb(طيِّب) so that's an Hadith(حديث).

615
00:37:27,337 --> 00:37:30,925
What about now let's talk about the Maana-Al-Urfi(معنی العرفی)

616
00:37:31,626 --> 00:37:33,133
the customary meaning of Jihad(جهاد).

617
00:37:33,946 --> 00:37:37,729
What meaning did Jihad(جهاد) pick up in the customs of people.

618
00:37:37,777 --> 00:37:43,942
So now, let's say that two men are talking in the first or second century of Islam.

619
